WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.110
Closing Ceremony at 9
In the Auditorium

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.490
All the characters in that <i>Dub Tone</i> show 
you recommended are so cute, Arisu-chan!

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:16.330
I liked the story in that <i>Sweetness and Champion</i> 
show Erika-senpai told me about.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:20.490
Speaking of story, that show <i>Ange Visual</i> 
Miko-chan wanted me to see was good, too.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.460
You're all about anime these days.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.990
So are you going to be watching anime 
all throughout summer break, too?

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.750
Of course, that's my plan.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:31.550
That's not all we're doing 
this summer, though.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.630
<i>That thing</i> is coming up this summer.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:35.830
Yes.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.260
<i>The thing</i>.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.510
The thing?

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.560
About our plans for summer break...

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.490
We're all going to <i>the thing</i>, right?

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.490
You mean <i>that thing</i>, correct?

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.620
The thing by the sea.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.330
The mid-summer ceremony.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.250
Or shall we call it the festival of desire?

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:35.300
Um, sorry, what do you mean by "the thing"?

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.260
What's this?

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.370
They're catalogs for <i>the thing</i>.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:40.880
Read this for details.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.140
Do I have to read <i>all</i> of this?

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:49.210
Reading all of the catalogs 
is a classic otaku pastime.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.890
Nah, that's a bit of a stretch.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.570
Just read the parts that are bookmarked.

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:59.320
Don't you worry, I'll give 
you all the support you need.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.950
"Notes on entering:

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.480
Wait in the entry line 
until the venue is open.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.150
Nearby transit facilities will be"...

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:13.830
Yes?

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.960
I brought you watermelons.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.590
Oh, you're studying.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.220
Yeah, studying.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:26.140
Hey, Onee-chan, do we have folding chairs?

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.460
Like the ones you use outdoors?

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.020
Yeah.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.350
We need some for our club.

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.600
Are you going camping or something?

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.100
Well...

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.730
The thing by the sea.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.030
We're going to an event at the sea.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.110
Huh, a sea festival or something?

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.570
So around Odaiba, then?

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:43.870
Yeah, that's it.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.250
There are going to be a ton of people there.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.690
Wow, the anime club does those 
kinds of events, too, huh?

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:54.100
Arisu-chan told me we should have 
folding chairs for when we're waiting.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.390
I see.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:56.940
I think they're in the closet.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.630
I'll get them for you later.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.810
Thanks, Onee-chan.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.640
Hey, camping?

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:13.020
No. Mii-chan's going to a sea festival 
at Odaiba with her anime club people.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.290
Wow.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:19.780
She seems to be having fun 
every day with her new friends.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:27.930
You're up early.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.850
I have to be on the first train 
in order to make it, apparently.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:31.560
Huh?

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.790
Dad's out?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:38.720
Yeah, he said he's meeting up 
with his friends by the sea.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.890
Okay, see you.

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:43.420
See you later.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:48.740
There's no one around 
at this time of the day.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:49.620
Oy.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:51.560
Neko-senpai.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.340
Don't scare me like that.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.400
<i>The thing</i> happens today, doesn't it?

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.310
Yes.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.190
I shall give you a word of warning.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:07.200
<i>Train arriving for Ikebukuro at Bay 1.</i>

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:10.870
When at war, the first to 
lower their guard is the first to die.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:11.830
Remember that.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.620
At war? It's not that big of a deal.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.710
I can't breathe!

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.220
E-Excuse me.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:29.460
Sorry.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.850
Pardon me, coming through.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:37.000
Please, sorry, coming through.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.610
Over here, Minoa.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.160
I thought I was going to die.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.400
The train was packed, wasn't it?

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.780
It's not any different from 
the train to school, is it?

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.370
Minoa, don't let your guard down; you'll die.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:53.910
It beckons me... my precious, 
also known as merchandise.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.670
It beckons me!

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:59.380
Musashisakai-senpai, you're way too hyper.

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:01.580
All right, let's get going.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.380
Do you have your sports drink, Minoa?

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:05.360
Yeah.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:07.360
It's important to avoid heat stroke.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.130
Right?

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.690
I don't think that'll be enough.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:14.750
What do you think this is?

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.190
This is a battlefield!

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.400
You may want to buy some more.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:22.400
I'll go buy some at the 
convenience store there, then.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.570
I'm worried, so I'll go check on her.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:33.530
O-Oh, no! I can't make it to the shelves.

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:36.280
That won't be an issue.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:37.610
Miko-chan.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:51.180
Kamiigusa Arisu is here, Ariake!

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.460
You're so hyped up, Arisucchi.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.630
You won't last the day.

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:58.010
I-I know.

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:00.170
But I'm just so excited.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:01.040
Right, Minoa?

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:01.920
Yeah.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.030
Okay, let's go.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:06.550
Isn't the venue over there?

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:08.070
Not so fast.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.400
You can't get in without lining up.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:18.450
Minoa.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:20.710
S-Sorry.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:23.050
It was an early morning.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:27.640
I know, you'd only ever be up so early 
during summer break for the Sunday Morning.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.230
The Sunday Morning?

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:32.560
He's talking about anime and tokusatsu 
shows that air on Sunday mornings.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.600
Oh, like <i>PreFae</i>.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:39.040
Sunday Morning has had children's 
shows since long before <i>PreFae</i>.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.230
It's a historically rich time period.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:42.920
That's not all.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:46.680
The many tokusatsu shows that set 
young boys' hearts ablaze

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.700
are part of the Sunday Morning!

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:53.890
Well, we're the anime club, though, 
so setting aside tokusatsu shows...

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:56.490
Don't expect to see anything but kids' shows.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:02.080
There's plenty of carefully-made anime 
that captivate us anime otaku, too.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:07.880
There've been depictions of girls' 
friendships that had me bawling.

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:11.880
And then there are the heartrending scenes 
where the good-looking bad guy falls.

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:16.260
The ending dances get a lot of 
attention on PreFae too, don't they?

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:20.020
They often have idol 
choreographers working on them.

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:24.020
I knew about <i>PreFae</i>, but I 
never knew it was <i>that</i> amazing.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.990
There are some amazing action episodes, too.

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:26.800
Indeed!

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.770
There are creators who get their breaks with 
their amazing Sunday morning anime battle art.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:33.280
You get so excited when we're 
talking about battles, Kaikai.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:34.280
It's <i>Kai</i>!

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:42.820
Do any of you need to go to the washroom?

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:45.040
I'm still fine.

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:47.490
We should go while we're still fine.

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.670
It's an iron rule, Arisucchi.

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:52.440
O-Of course.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:53.420
Well, then...

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.430
I think I'll go, too, then.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.340
Which way are the washrooms?

00:08:58.340 --> 00:08:59.130
There.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:02.530
That's the washroom line.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:05.190
You have to line up to go 
to the washrooms, too?!

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:06.800
It's actually the biggest business here.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.400
Y-You're kidding.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.180
Of course. That's common sense.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.810
Let's go, Minoa.

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:22.850
I'm back.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.830
Let's go back, then.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:39.550
Uh... Are we lost?

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:42.600
N-Not to worry.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:43.720
Sebas!

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.850
You there! No sliding!

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:51.610
He's not coming.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.860
What do we do, Arisu-chan?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.370
Who is she?

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:04.730
Do you know her, Minoa?

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.180
No.

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:11.000
<i>She's pretty, and her outfit's so pretty.</i>

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:15.400
<i>Wait, I need to say something.</i>

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:16.260
<i>But what language?</i>

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.420
<i>English? French? German?</i>

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:22.560
<i>U-Um...</i>

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.140
Spit cakes.

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:26.260
Spit cakes?

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:27.770
Are you hungry?

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.350
You can speak Japanese?

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.780
Thank goodness.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:32.540
Yes.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:33.790
Okay, let's go.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:36.900
Um...

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.150
Wait.

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:41.910
We're looking for some people.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.950
<i>Am I being abducted?</i>

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.800
Hey, Minoacchi, Arisucchi.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:52.970
Over here.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.520
Senpai!

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.550
You took a while.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:03.280
These two were looking for you.

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:05.350
Oh, they were lost.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.900
Thanks for bringing them.

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.560
Uh, who is she?

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:12.560
She was lined up right behind us.

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.300
I need to go to the bathroom.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.450
Could you please hold my spot?

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:18.060
Okay, sure.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:22.570
We talked a bit when I left the line.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.330
Oh, really?

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:26.580
Thank you.

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:27.940
It's okay.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:30.600
It's important to help each 
other out when we're in trouble.

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:32.930
I can't believe you'd get lost when you're

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:35.300
with someone like Arisucchi, 
who's been here before—

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:36.450
I'm sorry.

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:41.760
I'm actually here for the first time.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.670
I shouldn't have acted like I knew things.

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.100
This would never have happened.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.350
Th-That's not true.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:51.900
Yes, I think you two would 
have gotten lost, either way.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.480
That's harsh.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.780
As a veteran, I should have come with you.

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:57.770
Miko...

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:01.290
Hey, you're here for the first time?

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.130
Just like me.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:04.280
Really?

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:05.170
Yes.

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:08.000
We were in trouble, but we overcame it.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:12.270
It wouldn't be good to go home with a 
sad experience on our first time here.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:13.890
You're so...

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:15.540
So let's have fun.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.500
It's a festival, after all.

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:18.680
You're right.

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:21.080
Thank you.

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:23.400
You're welcome.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:29.590
I'm surprised you remembered 
Minoa's face, though.

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:33.020
Not so much her face, but she had that on.

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:35.900
This?

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.650
I love <i>Ru:ZERO</i>!

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.680
It's huge in Beijing, too.

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.710
It's popular in Beijing, too?

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:43.670
Beijing?!

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:46.410
Oh, yeah, she said she's from Beijing.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.160
My name is Yang Beibei.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:52.150
I'm Asagaya Minoa.

00:12:52.150 --> 00:12:52.930
Nihao.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.920
I'm Kamiigusa Arisu.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:57.860
She came here for this event.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:12:59.660
That's amazing.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:01.300
People come from overseas, too?

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:04.970
It's the biggest otaku event in the world.

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:08.550
I've always been dying to come here.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:13.290
Wait, wasn't <i>Ru:ZERO</i> in the spring?

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.550
Are there no delays these days?

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:16.940
Almost none.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:23.940
I've heard that shows used to become popular 
six months to a year after disc sales.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:25.950
It's at the same time nowadays, huh?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.320
It's a problem, sometimes.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:29.200
It is?

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:32.430
When I tell Japanese 
people that I like anime,

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:34.960
they deliberately bring up older shows.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.210
Even though I want to 
talk about current shows.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.750
So their kindness ends up hurting you.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.820
Where do you get information on anime?

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.210
Mostly online.

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.710
It's just like us.

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:50.850
I see the hype in Japan, and I'm 
like, "I know, it's so good!"

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:52.900
You can read Japanese?

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:56.100
Well, I guess we're having a 
normal conversation right now.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.400
Yes, I'm studying Japanese.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.360
So I can watch the anime I love.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:04.360
I met a few people in the US who 
could hold simple conversations.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:05.770
Wow.

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:08.860
Anime's connecting people around the world.

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:10.010
Yup.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:12.370
The world is connected through anime.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:16.270
Beibei-san, would you like to come with us?

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:17.420
Really?

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:19.170
Yes, gladly!

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:21.880
Now we just have to wait for the opening.

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:30.390
It's so hot...

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:31.790
The sun's rising.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.640
It's getting hotter.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.140
And this humidity...

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.300
Beibei-chan, are you o—

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.500
That's much cooler.

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:45.740
Japanese cooling products are excellent.

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:48.080
You're more prepared than we are.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:51.200
At least we aren't in direct sunlight.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:51.910
Look.

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.290
K-Kaikai-senpai!

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.790
Why is he in the sun?

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:00.290
You won't get me...

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:02.920
You won't get me, damn it!

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:05.750
Line problems.

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:23.130
Okay, it's about to begin.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:38.000
<b>Beibei, Don't Go</b>

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:48.080
It's been half an hour 
since we were applauding.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:50.380
It should be about another hour.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:51.800
An hour?!

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.820
We still can't go in!

00:15:57.340 --> 00:15:59.660
Just a little longer, Minoa.

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:01.750
Just a little longer.

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:04.650
I'm dying.

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:07.880
The treasure is in sight, everyone.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:11.750
Pass out now, and you'll 
be <i>re</i>starting back at home.

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:13.670
Huh?

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:16.050
What's going on?

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:17.360
It's an event favorite.

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:19.160
The staff's general warnings.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:22.150
Be sure to stay hydrated 
so you don't collapse.

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:25.390
You won't find Akina-sama from <i>Anosuba</i> here.

00:16:25.390 --> 00:16:28.350
You won't be getting any 
water over your heads.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:31.180
The staff are nerds, too.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.840
It kind of makes the heat more tolerable.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:42.100
It's time, Minoa.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:44.560
It was a long time coming.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.150
Yes, but our long journey is finally over.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:49.820
At last, we're setting foot.

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:52.070
In this new world.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:56.450
Arisu-chan, my heart's pounding.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:57.940
Mine, too.

00:16:57.940 --> 00:16:59.440
But don't be afraid.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:02.450
Let's open a new door together, Minoa.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.710
Yeah, Arisu-chan.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:12.730
You there, please follow the others inside.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:15.220
Cosplay Area  West Hall 1  East Hall  Industry Booths  West Floor 1

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:16.980
We're finally inside.

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:18.170
Exhausting, huh?

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:20.470
Let's split up, then.

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:26.100
The time has come for me to use 
my Unchained Golden Wallet!

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.350
All right, here we go.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.730
Just you wait, <i>Shikabari</i> merch!

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.280
That way?

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:31.370
I'll use this elite item to hunt you all down!

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:29.400
That way.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:40.870
There are so many people.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:43.600
Let's see, where is the <i>Ru:ZERO</i> merchandise?

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.370
Fliers.

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:47.120
Please and thank you.

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:49.000
Thank you.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:52.250
Unlimited
Fantasy world

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:50.770
Bags.

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:52.250
So cute.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.510
This is awesome, people are 
giving me so much stuff.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:55.450
Me, too.

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:56.880
Look what I got.

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.010
New show starting in fall.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.260
Paper fans.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:01.890
<b>Shikabari</b>

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:01.890
Take one, please.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.770
These are free.

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:05.450
I-It's so heavy.

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:07.760
They're digging into my shoulders.

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:10.580
Of course it'd be heavy 
if you took everything.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:12.270
You could have told us!

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.900
I bought it!

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:20.700
I'm so glad it wasn't sold out.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.740
You worry too much, Minoa.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:23.660
Oh?

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:28.420
Who was it that was grasping your 
wallet with a terrified face?

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:31.360
I'm glad we all got what we wanted.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:32.650
I know.

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:34.610
Can we get a photo together?

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:35.920
Of course.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:38.930
Okay.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.920
Come in closer, Minoa.

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:42.230
You, too, Miko.

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:43.460
Here we go, guys.

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:44.310
Smile!

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:49.120
Saori-san.

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:52.440
Hey.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.420
Hey, what's up?

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.670
Senpai, which college is she from?

00:18:57.670 --> 00:19:00.910
Oh, no, she's a cosplay buddy.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.680
She's a fresh young high schooler.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:03.950
"Fresh young"?

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:07.210
Nice to meet you, I'm Mutsuki.

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:10.210
As you can see, I'm from the 
Jouhoku High School Anime Club.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:11.410
I'm Erika.

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:14.840
I'm technically the president of the 
anime club at Sakaneko High School.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.740
The anime club at Sakaneko?

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:18.480
Oh, I've heard about it.

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:19.590
It's prestigious, isn't it?

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:21.890
Wait, is it not?

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:27.890
A Sakaneko graduate told me that 
their anime club was amazing.

00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:29.260
Huh...

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:36.070
There's just so many people, though.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.420
Obviously.

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:39.570
There are almost 200,000 people here.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.050
Two hundred thousand?!

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:42.070
That many?

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:45.080
<b>Forest
Conservation
Fund</b>

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:45.080
Six hundred thousand people in total 
over three days, apparently.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.580
You sure know a lot, Beibei-san.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:51.330
No wonder we have to be in line for 
hours, with so many people here.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:54.430
Lining up to get in, lining 
up once you're in...

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:57.090
It's the harshest event in Japan.

00:19:57.310 --> 00:19:58.960
I'm so happy, though.

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:00.590
Happy?

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:04.330
There are so many of my own kind here.

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:07.550
People who love anime and who I can 
get excited over the same anime with.

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:11.100
That makes me happy.

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:16.410
Being in line was tough, but I can handle it 
since I know I have a lot of friends here.

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:18.800
Plus I got to meet you guys.

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:20.230
Beibei-chan...

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:22.110
Yeah.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.850
I'm glad I got to meet you, too.

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:25.670
Me, too.

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:26.370
Yup.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:29.020
Cool, we're all here.

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:30.620
All right, want to head home?

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:33.460
Shouldn't we wait for Nakano-senpai?

00:20:34.070 --> 00:20:36.440
I guess I'll leave him a LINE 
message saying we're leaving.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:38.250
What about you, Beibei-chan?

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:41.720
I want to stay here a little longer.

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.630
I'll go wander around.

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:45.090
Okay.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:50.460
Minoa, Arisu, Miko, Erika, thank you!

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:53.970
Thank you, too.

00:20:53.970 --> 00:20:55.360
Bye-bye.

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.790
Good day.

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.220
I forgot to ask for her contact info.

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:01.140
Oh, yeah.

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:02.650
We screwed up.

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:06.670
And we just became friends.

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:08.910
It's all right.

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:12.680
As long as we're anime lovers, 
we'll meet here again.

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:14.410
Yeah.

00:21:14.970 --> 00:21:17.790
All right, we should go do 
<i>that thing</i> on our way home.

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:20.040
Agreed, Erika-senpai.

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:20.950
<i>That thing</i>?

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:26.900
This is so nice.

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:32.560
<i>Lining up sucked, but I bought my 
merchandise, and I made a new friend.</i>

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:35.870
Anime events are fun, huh, Arisu-chan?

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:37.690
Yes, very.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:41.470
By the way, what happened 
to Musashisakai-senpai?

00:21:41.470 --> 00:21:43.060
Huh? Say what?

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:44.190
I can't hear you.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:50.450
<b>Shikabari</b>

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:53.500
Event Exclusive

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:53.500
<b>Sold Out</b>

00:23:27.450 --> 00:23:30.790
Don't expect to meet someone 
twice on the battlefield.

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:36.300
Next episode: "Someone Is Shrouded in Light."

00:23:36.300 --> 00:23:39.300
What light? Find out for yourself.
